                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>The Ninth Session of the North Atlantic Council was held at Lisbon, February
                    20–25, 1952. The main item on the agenda was the “Coordinated Analysis of NATO
                    Defense Plans.” The Council adopted the military force goals and production
                    targets suggested in a report submitted by the Temporary Council Committee
                    composed of Harriman of the United States, Plowden of the United Kingdom, and
                    Monnet of France. Firm goals were established for 1952 and provisional estimates
                    were made for 1953 and 1954. For documentation on the Ninth Session of the North
                    Atlantic Council, see <ref target="frus:frus1952-54v05p1/pg_107">volume V, Part
                        1, pages 107</ref> ff.</p>
            </div>
